1. User Journey

The user journey represents the step-by-step interaction of the user with the encryption tool.

- Start Menu: The user is met with the home screen of the website.
- Logging in or Registration: In order to have access to the tool, the user needs to create an account.
- Inserting Text: The user starts typing text in the input field.
- Saving File: The encrypted text will be available to view on the website and the user will have a choice to save it on their personal device.
- Decryption: After registration, a unique decryption key is generated for the user and is securely kept on a database. It can later be used to automatically decrypt messages. The user can load encrypted text and press "Decrypt" to restore original content.
- Setting a Custom Key: A separate window allows users to manually input a custom key for decryption.
- Clearing Text Boxes: A “Clear” button resets the text field, with a confirmation prompt to prevent accidental loss.

