2. Wireframe Diagram

The wireframe diagram displays each stage of the user interface from the user’s perspective.

Core interface components:

- Text input area for writing or pasting text.
- Encrypted text output box.
- Buttons: Encrypt, Decrypt, Set Key, Save Key, Save File, Clear Text.
- Status bar for user feedback (e.g., “Encryption successful”, “Key saved”, etc.).
- Simple top menu for “Help” or “About”.

3. System Architecture

The system will operate in two stages:

	3.1 Local Prototype (Current Stage)

	- Python-based desktop app using tkinter for UI and cryptography (Fernet or AES) for encryption.

	- Saves encrypted text and key locally.

	3.2 Final Web Version (Future Stage)

	- Built with Flask for backend logic.

	- Uses RSA encryption for login/registration.

	- HTTPS secured connection with SSL/TLS for data protection.

	- Deployed on a Raspberry Pi server using port forwarding for remote access.

	- Protected with universal firewall and Fail2Ban to prevent unauthorized login attempts.

This design ensures that the transition from local encryption to a fully online encrypted system remains smooth and secure.


